 "note": "Each home grows a tree of Wide forks (half-turn symmetry): a trunk relay, a fork into two limbs, and a fork on each limb whose twigs reach the middle line. Both trees' inner twigs meet at the T4 hill; their outer twigs meet at the top and bottom canopy relays, which retract them. The trunk relay drops the trunk; two root platforms keep each home on its limbs. [KEEP edit 2026-11-11: trunk retracts -> laser relays; canopy retracts -> launchers (targets: both upper / lower limbs + the hill).]",
 "geometricSymmetry": true,
 "labVariant": {
  "junctions": true
 },
 "experimental": true,
 "ruleWaivers": {
  "S03": "half-turn symmetry: the front door (camera side) is the same for both seats, so the sim walk from each home differs by a few seconds - the same as the live point-symmetric pool maps N-11 / N-14 / N-20 / N-22 / N-24 / N-28 (first measured 2026-10-28, junction fairness walk); pending Daniele",
  "S04": "half-turn symmetry: the front door (camera side) is the same for both seats, so the sim walk from each home differs by a few seconds - the same as the live point-symmetric pool maps N-11 / N-14 / N-20 / N-22 / N-24 / N-28 (first measured 2026-10-28, junction fairness walk); pending Daniele",
  "N16": "each canopy relay drops its own side's outer twig (the other side's twig is fixed, so the relay stands on two fixed decks) - the tree's idea; pending Daniele"
 },
